{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1980,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e DEREK: How did Celsius define his scale?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4320,
    "dDurationMs": 6620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e MICHAEL: Uh... He took the temperature water freezes at and said that's zero and then he took the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10950,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "temperature it boils at and says that's a\nhundred. And he figured a hundred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14730,
    "dDurationMs": 3809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was a good amount of demarcations to make in between the two.  Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18540,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e DEREK: Yeah. Except that's not what he did.\n\u003e\u003e MICHAEL: Really?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20700,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e DEREK: Celsius never devised nor used the scale that now bears his name."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25140,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e MICHAEL: Are you kidding me?  \n\u003e\u003e DEREK: No, Michael, I'm not!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28140,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the Swedish town of Uppsala,\nlocated 70 kilometers north of Stockholm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32820,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is the house where Celsius lived.\nIn 1741 he was professor of astronomy at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38460,
    "dDurationMs": 6570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uppsala University. And this is the\nfirst ever Celsius thermometer... or is it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45660,
    "dDurationMs": 8910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e This is the first scale of Anders Celsius\nadded onto... or, added onto an old"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54570,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thermometer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55590,
    "dDurationMs": 6660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we have Delisle' scale on the left\nhand side and Celsius' new scale in the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62360,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e DEREK: These few markings show that Celsius came up with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the idea of separating the freezing and\nboiling points of water by 100 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70080,
    "dDurationMs": 5850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He made his first observations with the\nscale on Christmas Day 1741. But have you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75930,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "noticed something strange about this scale?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78600,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, 50 is marked in the middle but\nthe numbers increase down towards the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83250,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bulb of the thermometer. So, Celsius had\nhis scale upside down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87450,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He set zero degrees at the boiling\npoint of water and a hundred at the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91770,
    "dDurationMs": 1169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "freezing point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92939,
    "dDurationMs": 3331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why would he do this? Well, for one thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96270,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Celsius was just following the\nconvention of the other scale on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99240,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thermometer. Delisle' scale also had\nzero degrees for the boiling point of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102600,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "water increasing down to 150 for his\nfreezing point. And a likely reason both"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107340,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of them used upside down scales is\nbecause they avoid negative numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111600,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Sweden it gets much colder than freezing\nbut never warmer than boiling water so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116070,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you don't have to worry about pesky\nminus signs and this helps avoid logbook"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119909,
    "dDurationMs": 871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "errors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120780,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it would be really weird if you\nhad water boiling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123960,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "zero degrees and freezing at a hundred.\nWouldn't that be strange?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128520,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although it might seem strange today,\nthere is no objectively good reason for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132780,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "preferring an ascending scale over a\ndescending one for measuring degrees of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137100,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something, like hot or cold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139440,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, when Celsius died of\ntuberculosis in 1744, he was still using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144180,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this inverted scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146040,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So who reversed it? Who do we have to\nthank for the modern Celsius temperature scale?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150780,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well in 1745, just a year after Celsius'\ndeath"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154350,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a new column appears in the Uppsala\ntemperature record using the modern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158310,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scale and at the top it's got the\nheading \"Ekström\"  Now Ekström was the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162120,
    "dDurationMs": 5369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instrument maker at Uppsala.  In 1747\nanother column is added with the heading"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167489,
    "dDurationMs": 3631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Strömer who was Celsius' successor\nas professor of astronomy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171630,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, it's got the same modern scale.  But it's another professor at Uppsala who"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176610,
    "dDurationMs": 2129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "claims that he reversed the scale:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178860,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the famous biologist Carl\nLinnaeus. He says he reversed the scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182910,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when he ordered a thermometer from\nEkström for his greenhouse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186030,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whoever it was, we know that by 1745\nthere was an operational thermometer at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190410,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uppsala University with a scale that we\nnow all know as the Celsius temperature scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195690,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except... this was not the first such\nthermometer ever created.  In 1743 the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202290,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year before Celsius died, a French\nscientist working independently in Lyon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206310,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "created a thermometer with zero degrees\nat the freezing point of water and a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209850,
    "dDurationMs": 1889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundred at the boiling point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211739,
    "dDurationMs": 6391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his name was Jeane Pierre Christin. \nSo why isn't it called a degree Christin instead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218130,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a degrees Celsius?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219870,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, for a long time this temperature\nscale wasn't referred to using either of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224760,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their names and instead it was just\ncalled the \"centigrade scale,\" meaning a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228450,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundred steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229620,
    "dDurationMs": 3869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem with this was \"centigrade\"\nhas other meanings in French, Spanish and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233489,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Italian, where a grade specifically\nrefers to one one-hundredth of a right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237959,
    "dDurationMs": 4081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "angle. So to eliminate this confusion the\nInternational Bureau of Weights and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242040,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Measures in 1948 decided to rename the\ncentigrade scale after a scientist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246870,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bringing it into alignment with other\ntemperature scales like Kelvin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250140,
    "dDurationMs": 5310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Fahrenheit. They chose Celsius\npossibly due to a popular 1800's German"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255450,
    "dDurationMs": 3659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chemistry textbook by a guy named Berzelius. In it, Berzelius identified"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259109,
    "dDurationMs": 4021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Celsius as the first to devise a\ntemperature scale with zero at water's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263130,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "freezing point and a hundred at its\nboiling point propagating the myth that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266580,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Celsius created this scale. So is Celsius\nundeserving of having his name"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271740,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "immortalized on weather maps around the world?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274110,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, no. I mean making two marks and\ndeciding on a number of degrees in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279000,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between them that is the easy part which\nothers could, and as history shows, did do..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283410,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but what Celsius did was he established\nwhich physical processes could reliably"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287760,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "produce a fixed temperature. At the time\nwhen he was working, there were some 30"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292260,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "different temperature scales in use. Some\nthermometers had 18 different scales on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296970,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them, some more reliable than others. For\nfixed reference points one scale used the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301830,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deepest cellar of the Paris observatory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304350,
    "dDurationMs": 4319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "others used the melting temperature of\nbutter, the internal temperatures of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308669,
    "dDurationMs": 5731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "certain animals, or the hottest day in\nsummer in Italy, Syria or Senegal. These"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314400,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dubious scales combined, with\ninconsistent thermometer construction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317790,
    "dDurationMs": 4439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made recording accurate temperatures\nnearly impossible, not to mention sharing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322229,
    "dDurationMs": 4411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those temperatures with other scientists\nelsewhere. Celsius solved this problem in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326640,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a number of ways: he demonstrated that\nmelting snow maintains a fixed temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331340,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regardless of latitude or ambient\npressure. He also determined the precise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335910,
    "dDurationMs": 3509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relationship between boiling point of\nwater and the ambient pressure, so that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339419,
    "dDurationMs": 2611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thermometers could be calibrated under\nany conditions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342030,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He made it possible to establish a\nuniversal reliable system of temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346360,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measurement and this is why Celsius' name is a unit of temperature, even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350700,
    "dDurationMs": 5310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though the scale itself was not created\nby him and in fact today the Celsius"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356010,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scale is no longer defined by either of\nwater's phase transition points, instead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361080,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is based off the Kelvin scale and\nthat scale is defined by setting the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365010,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "triple point of water,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366120,
    "dDurationMs": 6090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where solid, liquid, and gas all exist in\nequilibrium at exactly 273.16 Kelvin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372210,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This fixes the size of a degree Kelvin,\nwhich is exactly the same as the size of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376740,
    "dDurationMs": 5210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a degree Celsius. The zero point of the\nCelsius scale is set a 273.15 Kelvin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381950,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what all this means\nis that today pure water boils at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386270,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "99.974 degrees Celsius and freezes at negative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390410,
    "dDurationMs": 6450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "0.0001 Celsius. This precision in a\nnearly universal system of temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396860,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measurement is thanks to a huge number\nof scientists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the C after the degree symbol\nstands not only for Celsius or Christin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405200,
    "dDurationMs": 5850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or Carl Linnaeus, but for the community\nof scientists whose work over centuries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411050,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made a scale so robust that we take it\nfor granted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414740,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[sound effects]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418540,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey! I hope you enjoyed that\nvideo. I just wanted to talk to you for a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421220,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "second about Patreon. Now, as you probably know, Patreon is a website where you can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425060,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "support creators that you like by\npledging a small dollar amount per month"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429080,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or per video. Now, I have had a Patreon\npage for a very long time but I have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433460,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "never promoted it and I have never\naccepted any pledges on that page."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437210,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reason is because I felt I could\nnever really offer value through the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440870,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "site because I was too disorganized and\nI was traveling too much, but despite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445160,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that 750 of you have pledged \nnearly $2000 a video and for that I"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450020,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "am incredibly grateful and I want to\nannounce that starting next video I will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454040,
    "dDurationMs": 5550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be accepting pledges through Patreon.\nAnd in return I will be offering some unique"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459590,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rewards to those patrons and I will also\nredouble my efforts to make this YouTube"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464450,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "channel bigger and better than it's ever\nbeen before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467660,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want to support Veritasium\ndirectly, you can now do that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470660,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "via Patreon and if you don't want to or you\ncan't that is totally fine too. Frankly, I"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475880,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "am just very appreciative that anyone\nlikes watching these videos at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479570,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now I'm going to go get to work on\nmaking this YouTube channel as good as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483440,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it possibly can be and I really want to\nthank you for all your support over the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486980,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years and I want to thank you for\nwatching!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
